{
  "hypothesis": "Further improve memory locality and loop order by reorganizing the loops to process points in a more cache-friendly manner and using blocking techniques. Specifically, we will focus on reducing the number of times distances are updated and sorted.",
  "transformations": [
    "Reorder the loops to minimize cache misses by processing blocks of points together.",
    "Reduce the frequency of sorting operations by maintaining a running list of k nearest neighbors."
  ],
  "sources_kept": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "src/knn.c",
      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n\n#define BLOCK_SIZE 16\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float distance;\n    char label;\n} Neighbor;\n\nint compare_neighbors(const void *a, const void *b) {\n    return ((Neighbor *)a)->distance - ((Neighbor *)b)->distance;\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    Neighbor * neighbors = (Neighbor *) malloc(sizeof(Neighbor) * k);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        neighbors[i].distance = -1;\n        neighbors[i].label = -1;\n    }\n\n    for (int block_i = 0; block_i < n_groups; block_i += BLOCK_SIZE) {\n        int end_i = (block_i + BLOCK_SIZE > n_groups) ? n_groups : block_i + BLOCK_SIZE;\n        for (int i = block_i; i < end_i; i++) {\n            Group g = groups[i];\n\n            for (int block_j = 0; block_j < g.length; block_j += BLOCK_SIZE) {\n                int end_j = (block_j + BLOCK_SIZE > g.length) ? g.length : block_j + BLOCK_SIZE;\n                for (int j = block_j; j < end_j; j++) {\n                    float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n\n                    if (d < neighbors[k - 1].distance || neighbors[k - 1].distance == -1) {\n                        neighbors[k - 1].distance = d;\n                        neighbors[k - 1].label = g.label;\n\n                        qsort(neighbors, k, sizeof(Neighbor), compare_neighbors);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    char most_frequent = neighbors[0].label;\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (neighbors[i].label != neighbors[i - 1].label) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = neighbors[i - 1].label;\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = neighbors[i].label;\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(neighbors);\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/knn.h",
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\n#define BLOCK_SIZE 16\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float x;\n    float y;\n} Point;\n\ntypedef struct {\n    char label;\n    int length;\n    Point * points;\n} Group;\n\nvoid on_error() {\n    printf(\"Invalid input file.\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n}\n\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\" n_groups=%d \", &n) != 1) on_error();\n\n    return n;\n}\n\nPoint parse_point() {\n    float x, y;\n    if (scanf(\" (%f ,%f) \", &x, &y) != 2)  on_error();\n\n    Point point;\n    point.x = x;\n    point.y = y;\n\n    return point;\n}\n\nGroup parse_next_group() {\n    char label; \n    int length;\n\n    if (scanf(\" label=%c \", &label) != 1) on_error();\n    if (scanf(\" length=%d \", &length) != 1) on_error();\n\n    Group group;\n    group.label = label;\n    group.length = length;\n    group.points = (Point *) malloc(sizeof(Point) * length);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n        group.points[i] = parse_point();\n    }\n\n    return group;\n}\n\nint parse_k() {\n    int k;\n    if (scanf(\" k=%d \", &k) != 1) on_error();\n\n    return k;\n}\n\nfloat euclidean_distance_no_sqrt (Point a, Point b) {\n    return ((b.x - a.x) * ((b.x - a.x))) + ((b.y - a.y) * (b.y - a.y));\n}\n\nint compare_for_sort(const void *a, const void *b) {\n  return *(char*)a - *(char*)b;\n}"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "This experiment aims to improve memory locality and loop order by processing blocks of points together and reducing the frequency of sorting operations. A new Neighbor struct is introduced to store both distance and label, and a custom comparator for sorting neighbors is defined."
}
